{#
 # The report can be read by an agent too: the same search, the same submission and the same chart,
 # served over MCP at /mcp. Nothing on a screen would say so, so a tab sticking out of the right edge of
 # every page does - set on its side, out of the way of what is read, since it is a side door and not
 # the report - and opens the one thing someone who wants to use it needs: how to add it to a client.
 #
 # It is the same `.pill` as everything closing the start page, a name on light ground and what is
 # said about it on dark, and the dialog is the one the raw output is shown in.
 #}
{% set endpoint = url('_mcp_endpoint_complexity_report') %}
{# permanent, so turbo carries it from page to page and it slides in once per visit rather than per click #}
<div class="mcp-teaser" id="mcp-teaser" data-turbo-permanent data-controller="mcp">
    <button type="button" class="pill mcp-teaser__badge" aria-haspopup="dialog"
            data-action="mcp#open">
        <span class="pill__name"><i class="fas fa-plug"></i> MCP server</span>
        <span class="pill__value pill__value--state">Connect</span>
    </button>

    <dialog class="raw mcp" aria-labelledby="mcp-title"
            data-mcp-target="dialog" data-action="click->mcp#dismiss">
        <div class="raw__head">
            <div>
                <div class="eyebrow">Model Context Protocol</div>
                <h2 class="raw__title" id="mcp-title">Ask your agent about complexity</h2>
            </div>
            <button type="button" class="raw__close" aria-label="Close" data-action="mcp#close">
                <i class="fas fa-xmark"></i>
            </button>
        </div>
        <div class="mcp__body">
            <p class="mcp__lead">
                Everything the report carries is also an MCP server: an agent can look repositories up,
                submit new ones and draw the same chart, right in the conversation. No account and no key
                are needed.
            </p>

            <ul class="mcp__tools">
                <li><code>repository_search</code> finds the repositories the report carries</li>
                <li><code>repository_submit</code> queues a GitHub repository for analysis</li>
                <li><code>complexity_chart</code> draws the interactive chart, in clients that show MCP apps</li>
            </ul>

            <section class="mcp__step">
                <h3 class="eyebrow">Server URL</h3>
                <div class="mcp__copy">
                    <code data-mcp-target="source">{{ endpoint }}</code>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn--secondary mcp__copy-button" data-action="mcp#copy">Copy</button>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="mcp__step">
                <h3 class="eyebrow">Claude.ai &amp; Claude Desktop</h3>
                <p>
                    <em>Settings → Connectors → Add custom connector</em>, then paste the server URL above.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section class="mcp__step">
                <h3 class="eyebrow">ChatGPT</h3>
                <p>
                    <em>Settings → Apps &amp; Connectors → Advanced settings</em>, turn on developer mode, then
                    <em>Create</em> a connector with the server URL above and no authentication.
                </p>
            </section>

            <section class="mcp__step">
                <h3 class="eyebrow">Claude Code</h3>
                <div class="mcp__copy">
                    <code data-mcp-target="source">claude mcp add --transport http complexity-report {{ endpoint }}</code>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn--secondary mcp__copy-button" data-action="mcp#copy">Copy</button>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section class="mcp__step">
                <h3 class="eyebrow">Cursor, VS Code &amp; others</h3>
                <p>Most clients read a JSON config like this (VS Code names the key <code>servers</code>):</p>
                <div class="mcp__copy mcp__copy--block">
                    <pre data-mcp-target="source">{{ {mcpServers: {'complexity-report': {url: endpoint}}}|json_encode(constant('JSON_PRETTY_PRINT') b-or constant('JSON_UNESCAPED_SLASHES')) }}</pre>
                    <button type="button" class="btn btn--secondary mcp__copy-button" data-action="mcp#copy">Copy</button>
                </div>
            </section>
        </div>
    </dialog>
</div>
